From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:34:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] GPU: a raw buffer view off 16 bytes gets its own copy
 (VICTORY_RAW_OWN_COPY=1); refused views are named

The host takes a raw buffer view on 16 bytes only (upstream #3540: another
one removes the device); the console takes any dword. Such a view was
refused and its slot read zeros: "buffer view the host would refuse left
null ... first=2 count=72 ... raw=true" and an unordered one of 1984 dwords
in the runs of 2026-11-27/28 (158 and 199 views left null).

With VICTORY_RAW_OWN_COPY=1 (off by default) a raw view that is on a dword
of its buffer's host copy but not on 16 bytes of it is made on a copy of
its own bytes, from byte 0: the path views off their copy's elements
already take (own_bytes, shadow::exact). Shader and unordered views, and
the copy a list brings up to date (buffer_copy), ask the same question.

Always: the first 8 refused views of each of six kinds are logged with
their heap slot, the title memory they read and the fields the host would
get, and a line with the frame line counts them by kind, with the
structured views that could not be made raw views (not on 16 bytes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
